1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''From the July 9, 2009''' ''Kitsap Sun'':
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ruth Ingred Nordquist, affectionately known as "Nana" to her family passed away on July 5th 2009.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ruth was born in Brooklyn, New York, moved to Kitsap County in 1920 and remained in the area for her entire life. She was married to Harry Knut Nordquist in 1936 and spent 47 wonderful years as a housewife and mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ruth loved the simple pleasures of spending time with friends and family. Her foremost joy was to watch the numerous accomplishments of her great-grandchildren. Her pride was evident in every conversation and was always presented
2 CONC  with a bright smile and a glimmer in her eyes.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ruth was a devoted friend, wife, mother, sister, aunt, grandmother and great-grandmother. She was preceded in death by her husband, mother Sena Nordland, Father Robert Erstad, stepfather Sverre Nordland, and siblings Lillian Thom
2 CONC son, Norman Erstad, and Margaret Kimball. She is survived by her daughter Barbara and son-in-law George Peichoto, grandson Eric Wagner and his wife Melissa, their children Ashley and Austin, grandson Leif Wagner, and numerous niec
2 CONC es and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT >The family would like to thank Dr. Michael Butler, the staff at Park Vista and Ridgemont Terrace. Their exceptional care of Ruth extended her time with us and gave her the quality of life she so rightfully deserved.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ruth always presented herself with style, dignity and grace. She dearly loved all those around her and the memories of our time with her will be cherished forever. Services will be held at Miller Woodlawn Funeral Home located at 
2 CONC 5505 Kitsap Way, Bremerton, WA 98312 on Tuesday July 14, 2009 at 2 p.m.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.kitsapsun.com/news/2009/jul/09/ruth-ingred-nordquist-0/#axzz2tmcUJ741 Kitsap Sun: Ruth Ingred Nordquist, 91]
