1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Name:	Ronald I. Nordquist Gender:	Male Death Age:	71 Birth Date:	26 May 1936 Birth Place:	Bremerton Residence Place:	Pearl Harbor, Hawaii Death Date:	16 May 2008 Death Place:	Eugene Burial Date:	23 May Burial Place
2 CONC :	Bremerton, Wash. Father:	 Ivar Nordquist Mother:	 Margaret Nordquist Siblings:	 Wshington California
2 CONT
2 CONT May 26, 1936 - May 16, 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be held for Ronald I. Nordquist, 71, of Coos Bay, at 11 a.m. on Wednesday, May 21, at the Gloria Dei Lutheran Church, 1290 Thompson Road in Coos Bay. Interment will be Friday, May 23, in Bremerton, Wash.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ronald was born May 26, 1936, in Bremerton, to Ivar and Margaret (Warren) Nordquist. He died May 16, 2008, in Eugene.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ron spent his younger years in many different locations with his mother, stepfather and three sisters including California, Wshington and Hawaii. He joined the U.S. Navy in 1956, and served onboard the USS Newell, stationed out of
2 CONC  Pearl Harbor, Hawaii.
2 CONT
2 CONT He met his wife, Barbara "BJ" Nordquist, while he was stationed in Long Beach, Calif. They made their home in Whittier, Calif., for 34 years. They lived in New Jersey for nine years and retired to Coos Bay in 2003.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ron enjoyed camping, hunting, stamp collecting and working in his garden.
2 CONT
2 CONT He will be greatly missed by his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife of 50 years, Barbara; daughter, Hallie Espinosa; son, Ron Nordquist and wife, Karen Daughtery of North Bend; son, Lars and wife, Karen Nordquist of McKinney, Texas; five grandchildren, Breanna Nordquist,
2 CONC  Chance Espinosa, Hunter Nordquist and Max and Jacksen Nordquist; two brothers, Gary Nordquist and wife, Linda and Bob Brown and wife, Sherri; three sisters, Diane and husband Ted Ingersall, Susan and husband, Tom Brockett and Deb
2 CONC bie and husband, Steve Bahnsen; many beloved nieces, nephews and cousins; and his faithful dogs, Shady and Chip.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his father, Ivar; mother, Margaret; stepfather, Jesse Warren; stepmother, Bertie Nordquist; stepmother, Lil Nordquist; and best friend, Earl Rasanen.
