1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''John made one final update to his Geni profile a few weeks before he died. It is preserved below in his memory.''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.kitsapsun.com/obituaries/pbks0619791 Obituary]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Update: I have stage four pancreatic cancer and a few months left. I'm released my profiles to David Scott Pelkey on October 13, 2023. Farewell and God bless.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pelkey - in 2007, I received a family journal as an inheritance from my mother, although it was from my father's side. It began in 1775 with the marriage of Anne White, the daughter of John White, to David Burnes, the fella w
2 CONC ho sold Washington DC to George. The journal contained the births, marriages, and deaths of family members from the 1700s through the 1800s, with the final entry in 1911. In addition, from another family member now deceased, I got
2 CONC  the description of a family crest with what he thought were three pigs with muzzles above a chevron filled with flowers, or some such, related to John White.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Arms: A cheveron ermine between three bear's heads couped and muzzled, a crescent for difference, for Wight.] British History Online
2 CONT
2 CONT With the help of Byron Whitesides, a long lost cousin who convinced me I was spelling it wrong, I began researching the family called Wightt in Geni in 2014. Six years of research, with a break for the Hoyt family.
