1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary for Elaine Rosalie Eck Elaine Rosalie Ellis Eck was born in Davenport, Iowa on September 16, 1927 to Bryant T. and Navada O. Ellis. Elaine was the eldest of three children. A  brother, Bryant Jr., and sist
2 CONC er Mary Ann have preceded her in death. The Ellis  family relocated to Sheridan, Wyoming in the mid 1930's, where her father found  steady work. First as a blacksmith, then as a deputy sheriff, and finally as a  ranch owner in Cle
2 CONC armont, Wyoming. Elaine attended local schools in Clearmont, graduating from high school there in 1945. Not overly fond of Clearmont, nor the ranching life, Elaine went on to study nursing at the University of Wyoming. "Clearmont 
2 CONC wasn't hell, but you could see it from there", as she used to say.
2 CONT
2 CONT The University's nursing school program included a residency that was to be served  at the Deaconess Hospital in Great Falls, Montana. It was in Great Falls where  she met Edward Eck, an Army Air Corp pilot from Anaconda, who was 
2 CONC in flight  training for the Berlin Airlift. Upon graduation from nursing school in 1949, she became engaged to Edward, and they were married in December of 1950.  Ed and Elaine settled in Anaconda, where he joined his family's con
2 CONC struction  business, and she worked as a registered nurse for various doctors and medical  clinics. Sons Ted and David were born in 1953 and 1957. In 1960, Ed and  Elaine went on to operate Theodore Eck and Sons as a solely owned 
2 CONC entity.  They operated the construction business until the mid-1990s. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to the family construction business, Elaine was deeply involved in the  Anaconda Community, serving in many civic activities and organizations. Elaine  was a member of the American Association of University Women, the 
2 CONC Chi Omega Sorority, Eastern Star, Daughters of the Nile, the Community Concert Association, , and local chapter of  the P.E.O. Sisterhood. Forever dedicated to health care, Elaine donated a lot of her time to the Community Hospita
2 CONC l of Anaconda. She served on the hospital's board of directors, recruited doctors to the Anaconda area, and also helped oversee  the construction of the Anaconda's new Community Hospital. Elaine's personal  interests included read
2 CONC ing, sewing, gourmet cooking, and world travel. Elaine is  survived by her daughter-in-law Joann Eck, son David and his wife Patti. She was  preceded in death by husband Edward in 2015, and son Ted in 2008.  Elaine was grandmother
2 CONC  to Heidi Rasmussen, and husband Lars, and grandsons Carl and Justin Eck. She was great grandmother to Aksel, Freja, and Iver Rasmussen. 
