1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Efter avlagd studentexamen 1907 blev han volontär vid Positionsartilleriregementet, och efter officersexamen 1910 avancerade han där till löjtnant 1914 och kapten 1925. Två år senare övergick han till Smålands armé
2 CONC artilleriregemente. Han blev riddare av Svärdsorden 1931.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stiernspetz ingick i det svenska gymnastiklaget som tog guld i trupptävlan vid Olympiska sommarspelen 1912. Han avlade 1917 examen vid Gymnastiska centralinstitutet.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yngve_Stiernspetz
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Yngve Stiernspetz , born April 27, 1887 in Eksjö , died April 4, 1945 on Lidingö , was a Swedish military and gymnast .
2 CONT
2 CONT Yngve Stiernspetz was the youngest son of the railway engineer Herman Valentin Stiernspetz (1847–1917) and his wife Anna Maria Viktorine Hagström (1857-1939 ). After graduating in 1907, he became a volunteer with the Position Arti
2 CONC llery Regiment , and after graduating as an officer in 1910, he advanced there to lieutenant in 1914 and captain in 1925. Two years later, he transferred to Småland's Army Artillery Regiment . He became a knight of the Order of th
2 CONC e Sword in 1931.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stiernspetz was part of the Swedish gymnastics team that won gold in the team competition at the 1912 Summer Olympics . In 1917 he graduated from the Central Gymnastics Institute .
2 CONT
2 CONT Yngve Stiernspetz was from 1928 married to Vera Maria Sandström (1898-1986 ), daughter of the manager Esaias Johannes Sandström and Sigrid Maria Blommert.
