1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/census/person/pf01037997007197 FT 1865:] Ugift. Bor med far og stemor på Ringstad store i Tune
2 CONT
2 CONT Overtar halve Store Ringstad etter faren sammen med broren Ole . Ole overtar hans del i 1873.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/459/205 Marriage of Hans Martin Eskildsen and Olava Mathisdatter Minge 5 April 1867
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Martin Eskildsen (Ryen Minge) took over half of the Store Ringstad farm with his brother Ole Eskildsen Ringstad. He sold his part to Ole in 1873. He traveled with wife and 6 children to the US in May 1881. He was a lottery wi
2 CONC nner in Ryen in Tune, Ostfold, Norway in 1873. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Martin Eskildsen Ryen Minge (born 1841) immigrated to the United States in 1881 with his wife Olava Mathisdatter (Olava Martine Minge born 1845 whose family is from Minge, Tune, Ostfold, Norway) with their 6 children: Anne Ma
2 CONC rie (1968) Edvard Marentius (1870) Adolfine (1874) Hanna Jasefine (1876) Johannes (John Minge) (1878) Ole Alfred (1881).
2 CONT * See attached documents.  He changed his name to Martin Minge after immigrating to Otter Tail County, Minnesota, United States. He had 3 more children after immigrating to Minnesota, and his wife Olava died the same day she gave 
2 CONC birth to twins in 1886. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born with the name Hans Martin Eskildsen. In the 1875 Census in Norway his name is listed as Martin Eskildsen living in the city Ryen, Norway. When he immigrated to America in 1881, he went by the name Hans Martin Eskildsen Ryen. 
2 CONC In the 1885 Census and 1895 Census in Dane Prairie Township, Otter Tail County, Minnesota, USA, he went by the name Martin E. Ryen. His wife Olava Martine Mathisdatter Minge died at age 39 in 1886 after giving birth to twins (Carl
2 CONC  August Minge and Olava Martine Minge). Olava's family, including her father Mathias Olesen Minge and brother Fredrick Minge and her other family members lived next door to the family and probably helped raise Martin and Olava's c
2 CONC hildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After Olava's death, Martin and all of his children went by the last name Minge.In the 1900 and 1910 Census in Minnesota, USA, Martin and his children all use the last name Minge. He goes by the name Martin Minge after his wife di
2 CONC ed. In 1910 he lives with his daughter Adolphine Ringstad (Minge). He was a farmer living near many of his wife's family members. He never re-married. 
