1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT * Jewish
2 CONT * Memories of German super-inflation:
2 CONT # Mother would be waiting when Father had a patient and once paid would run out immediately and purchase something with the money.
2 CONT # A visit with Father to the cemetery; there was a slot for contributions to the poor that Father would have to stuff a lot of million notes into, with a stick available to push it in
2 CONT # When the Mark was stabilized, Father gave him a single Mark coin and told him this would now be good forever.
2 CONT * Bar Mitzvah memories 12/31/27 (New Year's Eve):
2 CONT # Got a gramophone (maybe from friend of Mother's, Amy Ritter) which his father had not wanted to get, but he really wanted. Relented and then couldn't wait to show him. Crank-up device. Schubert's Military Marches one of first re
2 CONC cords.
2 CONT # Three or four other boys Bar Mitvah'd at the same time.
2 CONT # Martha had wanted to do the party, but the parents hired a cook for the evening. Father's lab technician played the piano.
2 CONT # Nine silver pencils received as gifts.
2 CONT # Franz Apt gave him Schnitzler's five-volume books.
2 CONT # Got a fancy desk from the Parents.
2 CONT # Was Dad's actual Jewish birth date.
2 CONT # Second cousin stayed with them from Berlin. Fritz Lefebvre.
2 CONT * 1934 Summer, checked out Paris, not a good situation there.
2 CONT * 1936, 1937 - Worked at hospital in Vienna during summers
2 CONT * 1937 - Jaundice
2 CONT
